Hello @Darwin Osgood​ ​! I wanted to bring us back to this escalation record, as I see you have been communicating directly with the client by email, and CC'd the advocate and their manager. This has caused a disconnect, and some client confusion as well as the client is not able to be supported directly on this case, and the emails through outlook are not openly accessible to CRT so we can remain engaged on the development and next steps while we work towards a resolution.

I just wanted to make sure that CRT is able to support both you and the client properly, and CRT is engaged directly on the escalation record if additional support is needed for you or the client. We will then partner directly with our advocate and leadership to ensure full resolution and advocates work directly through salesforce/cases.

Here is where we currently stand on this incident:
Gabby reached out to the client 10/26 and the Client processed payroll to ensure employees are paid. We will partner with IT to grab additional examples of the errors they are seeing in the pay grid. We need live data in order to troubleshoot furtherWe will work to waive any fees associated with them submitting payroll past the cut off date for this pay period. 

@David Patten​  and myself will continue to support Gabby under case 07808332, and the client can reply directly to the email chain from that case.

Please let me know if you have any questions! Thank you. 

